              "date": "2026-04-24T10:05",
              "body": "3-mo f/u.\n\nFeels like himself. Back to daily walks. Urine normal color. No bruising, no nosebleeds. Anticoag clinic visits every 4 weeks now, in range. Taking folic acid. Cardiology note still not in; he has a cardiology visit planned for the summer.\n\nMeds: warfarin per clinic, metoprolol succinate 100, ASA 81, atorvastatin 40, lisinopril 20, pantoprazole 40, folic acid 1.\n\nExam: vitals as charted, BP at goal. Valve click crisp, irregularly irregular, rate 70s. Lungs clear. Abdomen soft. No edema.\n\nA/P\n- Valve-related hemolytic anemia: CBC, LDH today.\n- Mechanical AVR/AF on warfarin: INR today as well, clinic continues.\n- HTN/CAD/HLD: stable, BMP today; lipids at the fall physical.\n- GERD: stable.\nNext visit September; LDCT due in the fall."
